WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.969 --> 00:00:06.300
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie Happy Game Of
Thrones Day!

00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:10.060
this is my last bonus video before the Season
4 premiere.

00:00:10.060 --> 00:00:11.910
I think we were all about to explode from
excitement.

00:00:11.910 --> 00:00:12.910
here’s what’s going down.

00:00:12.910 --> 00:00:16.720
This will be my Top 10 Moments from Season
3 just as a final look back.

00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:21.269
Then at the end of the video I’m going to
go over the giveaway rules and what my Game

00:00:21.269 --> 00:00:24.960
of Thrones video schedule will be going forward.

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:28.289
Careful for season 3 spoilers if you’re
not caught up yet, but let’s not waste any

00:00:28.289 --> 00:00:29.289
time.

00:00:29.289 --> 00:00:30.550
Number 10 - Jon Snow Becomes A Man

00:00:30.550 --> 00:00:33.090
A seminal time in the life of any teenager.

00:00:33.090 --> 00:00:38.420
This wasn’t so much Jon Snow losing his
virginity as it was Ygritte taking his virginity.

00:00:38.420 --> 00:00:43.370
You get the sense that she was the real brains
of that operation and Jon was just happy to

00:00:43.370 --> 00:00:44.370
oblige.

00:00:44.370 --> 00:00:46.100
It’s a nice reversal of gender roles.

00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:50.460
For instance, had everything played out in
King’s Landing and Ygritte been a member

00:00:50.460 --> 00:00:54.420
of the court, it would have been told from
a much more male perspective.

00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:58.880
Even though Cersei wields a lot of sexual
authority over men, she’s much much older.

00:00:58.880 --> 00:01:03.300
I don’t remember it being spelled out explicitly
in the books, but I think it’s implied that

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:07.760
when she was Jon Snow and Ygritte’s age,
Jaime was her only sexual partner.

00:01:07.760 --> 00:01:10.630
At least before she was married to Robert
Baratheon.

00:01:10.630 --> 00:01:15.010
As much fun as it was to watch that scene
in the cave, it was even better listening

00:01:15.010 --> 00:01:19.570
to Kit Harington and Rose Leslie talk about
how awful and awkward it was on set that day.

00:01:19.570 --> 00:01:24.710
I think that Kit Harington was also still
in a leg cast.

00:01:24.710 --> 00:01:28.630
So imagine him limping into that hot spring.

00:01:28.630 --> 00:01:30.570
Number 9 - Brienne Versus the Bear

00:01:30.570 --> 00:01:35.120
This was kind of a meta moment because first
off you have bad ass Brienne holding her own

00:01:35.120 --> 00:01:37.990
against a freaking bear with a wooden sword.

00:01:37.990 --> 00:01:38.990
So it’s just awesome.

00:01:38.990 --> 00:01:41.820
Then you have Jaime’s change of heart and
rescue.

00:01:41.820 --> 00:01:44.850
In reality it wasn’t his fighting skill
that saved them.

00:01:44.850 --> 00:01:46.869
He would have been shredded in seconds.

00:01:46.869 --> 00:01:51.360
It was just the threat of what Tywin Lannister
would do if he were hurt.

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:52.520
More than he had already been.

00:01:52.520 --> 00:01:57.220
I loved how the whole event invoked this classic
sense of chivalry that Brienne believed in

00:01:57.220 --> 00:02:00.200
so much.

00:02:00.200 --> 00:02:02.780
Most of the time she’s the one being chivalrous.

00:02:02.780 --> 00:02:05.210
But it was such a big moment for both of them.

00:02:05.210 --> 00:02:09.729
Brienne not dying and Jaime doing something
selfless for a change.

00:02:09.729 --> 00:02:11.730
Number 8 - The Night’s Watch Rebellion

00:02:11.730 --> 00:02:15.340
Dirty old Craster and the old Bear never saw
it coming.

00:02:15.340 --> 00:02:19.510
First we have to acknowledge that it was Burn
Gorman of Torchwood authoring the debacle.

00:02:19.510 --> 00:02:22.320
That was a nice meta Doctor Who fandom moment.

00:02:22.320 --> 00:02:26.209
But then you have the oh shit realization
that with Jeor Mormont dead and the Night’s

00:02:26.209 --> 00:02:30.200
Watch in open revolt, who is going to get
everyone ready for the Wildling Attack.

00:02:30.200 --> 00:02:32.270
I’m not even talking about the Army itself.

00:02:32.270 --> 00:02:36.069
They don’t even have a chance against the
small raiding party that Jon Snow was part

00:02:36.069 --> 00:02:37.069
of.

00:02:37.069 --> 00:02:40.420
I think we all shared a collective moment
of triumph when Old Craster ate it.

00:02:40.420 --> 00:02:45.130
Quickly followed by the horror on Samwell’s
face before he grabbed Gilly and took off.

00:02:45.130 --> 00:02:48.450
Number 7 - Thoros of Myr Brings Back Beric
Dondarrion

00:02:48.450 --> 00:02:52.940
Flaming swords aside, this was a huge deal
because it established that the dead can be

00:02:52.940 --> 00:02:54.610
made whole again.

00:02:54.610 --> 00:02:59.620
Not just reanimated wights, but brought back
to their normal state.

00:02:59.620 --> 00:03:02.370
Beric Dondarrion said that there were some
side effects.

00:03:02.370 --> 00:03:06.340
Like pieces of you would get left behind each
time you came back.

00:03:06.340 --> 00:03:11.290
Melisandre is pretty amazed when she finds
out how many times Beric has been brought

00:03:11.290 --> 00:03:16.270
back, so it seems like each priest or priestess
of the Red God expresses their powers in different

00:03:16.270 --> 00:03:17.270
ways.

00:03:17.270 --> 00:03:21.370
I think she’ll be able to do it before Winds
of Winter or Dream of Spring is over.

00:03:21.370 --> 00:03:26.910
So anyone who’s worried about characters
dying.

00:03:26.910 --> 00:03:30.010
As long as they’re in proximity to someone
with the powers of the Red God, there’s

00:03:30.010 --> 00:03:33.230
always a chance they’ll be brought back.

00:03:33.230 --> 00:03:35.160
Number 6 - Jon Snow Climbs The Wall

00:03:35.160 --> 00:03:39.300
This was one of the biggest action set pieces
of the season and involved a lot of really

00:03:39.300 --> 00:03:40.300
cool CG integration.

00:03:40.300 --> 00:03:44.050
I remember reading about the sheer size of
the Wall in the books.

00:03:44.050 --> 00:03:47.650
But until the show came along you really just
had to imagine what it looked like in your

00:03:47.650 --> 00:03:48.660
head.

00:03:48.660 --> 00:03:52.280
I think they did a great job of interpreting
just how massive it is.

00:03:52.280 --> 00:03:55.580
In the books George RR Martin made it 700
feet tall.

00:03:55.580 --> 00:03:58.920
And I feel like it becomes a whole character
in and of itself.

00:03:58.920 --> 00:04:01.720
Like the wall is a character in the story.

00:04:01.720 --> 00:04:05.879
All I can think about now is one, when are
we going to get to see or read about it being

00:04:05.879 --> 00:04:11.080
built and two, will we ever see someone blow
the true horn of winter and bring it crashing

00:04:11.080 --> 00:04:12.080
down.

00:04:12.080 --> 00:04:17.470
It’s still just a legend that blowing the
horn will destroy the wall.

00:04:17.470 --> 00:04:19.750
Let me know if you think we’ll see this
happen at some point.

00:04:19.750 --> 00:04:23.460
Number 5 - Ramsay Snow Tortures Theon for
an entire Season.

00:04:23.460 --> 00:04:29.130
The final act of torture was clearly the worst,
but there’s no promise after that the tortue

00:04:29.130 --> 00:04:31.880
won’t continue into the early part of season
4.

00:04:31.880 --> 00:04:34.660
So as far as we know, he’s still being tortured
right now.

00:04:34.660 --> 00:04:38.970
As bad as Theon was before Season 3, I feel
like he’s endured enough.

00:04:38.970 --> 00:04:42.470
Everything about the character as he is right
now just makes you feel sorry for him.

00:04:42.470 --> 00:04:46.630
Sorry for the circumstances that made him
feel like he had to betray his adopted family

00:04:46.630 --> 00:04:49.710
and sorry for what Ramsay Snow has done to
him.

00:04:49.710 --> 00:04:52.130
There is the promise that he’ll get out
eventually.

00:04:52.130 --> 00:04:58.530
There was footage from the trailer with Theon
on horseback and he wasn’t running away.

00:04:58.530 --> 00:05:00.300
Number 4 - Sam Kills White Walker

00:05:00.300 --> 00:05:07.330
I remember the first time I saw this, I had
to rewind and watch it again because I couldn’t

00:05:07.330 --> 00:05:10.790
tell if he dropped the obsidian dagger before
he ran off with Gilly.

00:05:10.790 --> 00:05:16.710
Samwell for all his faults is one of the first
new people to figure out that one of the White

00:05:16.710 --> 00:05:19.720
Walkers’ biggest weaknesses is Obsidian
or dragon glass.

00:05:19.720 --> 00:05:21.010
Whatever you want to call it.

00:05:21.010 --> 00:05:27.650
I’m really hoping that he’s able to educate
the rest of the Night’s Watch in time.

00:05:27.650 --> 00:05:33.440
There was that ominous shot of the white walker
in one of the season 4 trailers.

00:05:33.440 --> 00:05:35.229
Number 3 - Jaime Hand Chopped Off

00:05:35.229 --> 00:05:39.330
This had to be the defining moment for the
first part of the season.

00:05:39.330 --> 00:05:43.890
The death of Ned Stark kind of already told
us that no one was safe, but getting his hand

00:05:43.890 --> 00:05:48.650
chopped off let you know that George RR Martin
and the show wasn’t afraid to permanently

00:05:48.650 --> 00:05:50.509
maim it’s lead characters.

00:05:50.509 --> 00:05:54.700
It’s such an oh shit moment just because
of the spectacle and because they just slammed

00:05:54.700 --> 00:05:57.050
to black right as Jaime started screaming.

00:05:57.050 --> 00:06:00.340
But it really made me wonder what the hell
was going to happen to the character.

00:06:00.340 --> 00:06:05.160
It’s not like they have hospitals and in
the books, the Brave Companions basically

00:06:05.160 --> 00:06:08.560
treat Jaime and Brienne like trash until they
made it back to Roose Bolton.

00:06:08.560 --> 00:06:11.120
Number 2 - Daenerys Becomes the Breaker of
Chains

00:06:11.120 --> 00:06:17.550
This mostly refers to her taking the Unsullied
and exacting revenge against Kraznys.

00:06:17.550 --> 00:06:23.580
It was one of those big moments that HBO teased
in all the clips.

00:06:23.580 --> 00:06:29.800
Her activating Drogon so to speak using High
Valyrian.

00:06:29.800 --> 00:06:35.240
It became this amazing CG sequence of her
burning everything in sight and marching away

00:06:35.240 --> 00:06:37.270
with this massive army.

00:06:37.270 --> 00:06:41.490
Such a huge win for her when you consider
that there’s so much civil war still going

00:06:41.490 --> 00:06:44.330
on in Westeros while all this is happening.

00:06:44.330 --> 00:06:46.520
Number 1 - The Red Wedding

00:06:46.520 --> 00:06:50.729
I don’t think there’s any Season 3 WTF
list that doesn’t list this as the number

00:06:50.729 --> 00:06:51.729
one moment.

00:06:51.729 --> 00:06:54.860
It was one of THE most talked about moments
on Television last year.

00:06:54.860 --> 00:06:58.660
And most people don’t even get HBO or watch
the show.

00:06:58.660 --> 00:07:02.600
Before this George RR Martin and the show
already had meme’s for slaughtering main

00:07:02.600 --> 00:07:04.000
characters wholesale.

00:07:04.000 --> 00:07:08.260
But the Red Wedding became this meta cultural
event for the world.

00:07:08.260 --> 00:07:11.050
First there were all the reaction videos,
like Maisie Williams.

00:07:11.050 --> 00:07:13.370
Queen of Vines.

00:07:13.370 --> 00:07:15.010
Then there were all the parodies.

00:07:15.010 --> 00:07:18.789
You can really gage the popularity of something
by how much it gets parodied.

00:07:18.789 --> 00:07:22.870
And just in terms of television, this was
the most parodied event all year.

00:07:22.870 --> 00:07:25.199
I think my favorite was probably Maisie Williams.

00:07:25.199 --> 00:07:29.800
Her reaction video was only six seconds, but
it perfectly summed up the spirit of every

00:07:29.800 --> 00:07:32.009
single other video that followed.

00:07:32.009 --> 00:07:33.009
But now it’s your turn.

00:07:33.009 --> 00:07:36.550
Let me know what your favorite season 3 moment
was and which event you're most looking forward

00:07:36.550 --> 00:07:39.370
to in season 4.

00:07:39.370 --> 00:07:40.780
Everyone is waiting on the edge of their seat
for the purple wedding.

00:07:40.780 --> 00:07:44.170
Which is funny because all the book readers
are kind of grumbling that George RR Martin

00:07:44.170 --> 00:07:46.880
never called it the purple wedding.

00:07:46.880 --> 00:07:50.600
Just another example of how pop culture can
take something and change it in the larger

00:07:50.600 --> 00:07:51.600
context.

